cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GitHub Country Classifier: Inferring a Developer's Country from Public GitHub Profiles"
abstract: >-
  A fine-tuned multilingual-e5-small classifier that infers the country (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, 245 classes) of a GitHub
  user from the public fields of their profile (location, company, blog, email domain, Twitter handle, bio), or
  abstains, shipped as a 45 MB int8 ONNX model with a trimmed vocabulary that runs locally in Node.js or the browser.
  Trained on 394,221 users whose declared locations were geocoded with Nominatim, plus users without a location
  labelled by email-domain rules and by a large language model, and GeoNames city names; 98.7% accuracy on 46,518
  held-out users with a location and 95.8% on held-out users without one whose profile names a place.
